# part: A5 - generators and properties
# dir: week5/solution
# load: :m + APL.AST APL.Tests Test.QuickCheck
? Run this several times. How many of the expressions are actually interesting?
generate (genExp 4)
generate (genExp 4)
generate (genExp 4)
? Size 0: what can a generator produce when it has no size budget left?
generate (genExp 0)
? The printer, which the round-trip property depends on
printExp (Add (CstInt 1) (CstInt 2))
? A property that holds
quickCheck (\x -> x + 0 == (x :: Int))
? A property that does not. Read the shrunk counterexample, not just the failure.
quickCheck (\x y -> x - y == (y - x :: Int))
? classify shows the distribution that cover would make into a requirement
quickCheck (\x -> classify (x > (0::Int)) "positive" (x + 0 == x))
